From: Lupsa Alexandra <alexandra.lupsa1103@stud.acs.upb.ro>
Subject: [PATCH] prism: Fall back to read() when mmap() fails

pm_read_file() maps the source file with mmap() whenever
_POSIX_MAPPED_FILES is defined, and turns a failed mapping into a load
error. musl defines _POSIX_MAPPED_FILES, but Unikraft's ukmmap only
provides anonymous mappings and fails for any file descriptor, so every
Ruby file failed to load.

Fall back to pm_string_file_init(), which reads the file into memory.

Signed-off-by: Lupsa Alexandra <alexandra.lupsa1103@stud.acs.upb.ro>
---
diff --git a/prism_compile.c b/prism_compile.c
--- a/prism_compile.c
+++ b/prism_compile.c
@@ -11352,8 +11352,10 @@
 
     source = mmap(NULL, size, PROT_READ, MAP_PRIVATE, fd, 0);
     if (source == MAP_FAILED) {
+        // Not every platform that defines _POSIX_MAPPED_FILES can map
+        // regular files. Fall back to reading the file into memory.
         close(fd);
-        return PM_STRING_INIT_ERROR_GENERIC;
+        return pm_string_file_init(string, filepath);
     }
 
     close(fd);
